From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:45:13 +0000
Subject: usb: cdns3: cdnsp-plat: report a failed controller resume

cdns_resume() fails when the role does not restart after power loss.
The resume then returned 0, and the controller stayed unusable without
an error. Return the cdns_resume() result.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c
@@ -351,7 +351,7 @@ static int cdnsp_controller_resume(struct device *dev, pm_message_t msg)
 		return ret;
 
 	/* cdns_resume() may sleep; do not invoke it under cdns->lock. */
-	cdns_resume(cdns);
+	ret = cdns_resume(cdns);
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&cdns->lock, flags);
 	cdns->in_lpm = false;
-- 
Armbian

